### Practical 11: Containerization with Docker and Docker Compose
### REST Client Test Suite

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Root Metadata & Container Topology Inspection
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### 2. Live Docker Environment Telemetry
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/docker/status
Accept: application/json

### 3. Clear Cache & Event Logs
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cache/clear

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/events/clear

### 4. Register Container Developer Account
# @name registerUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Docker Orchestrator",
  "email": "docker_pilot@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 5. Login to Acquire JWT Token
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "docker_pilot@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Store token from login
@authToken = {{loginUser.response.body.token}}

### 6. Verify Authenticated Profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 7. Create Task in Containerized MongoDB
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Verify Docker Compose Multi-Container Stack",
  "description": "Ensure inter-container bridge network routes backend requests to mongodb service",
  "priority": "high"
}

@taskId = {{createTask.response.body._id}}

### 8. Fetch Tasks (Tests In-Memory Caching in Container)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 9. Update Task
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "completed": true,
  "priority": "medium"
}

### 10. Delete Task
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
